# How to cite this work. The README's "Licence" section states the
# attribution string derived from this file; CC-BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA) asks a
# reuser to reproduce it, and tests/test_citation.py fails when the two
# disagree or when `version` differs from the packaged version.
#
# This repository copy names no commit: a committed file cannot name the
# commit that contains it. The copy shipped in the release archive, once the
# release job builds one, will have the release's commit stamped into it.
#
# `date-released` is the date of this version's CHANGELOG.md heading;
# tests/test_citation.py fails when the two disagree.
#
# Unresolved: every PLACEHOLDER- value awaits the owner's chosen
# identity (pseudonym or real name, ORCID, affiliation). A build on a release
# tag fails while any of them remains.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these results or this software, please cite them as below.
  The same form is the attribution CC-BY 4.0 requires for the data.
type: software
title: wave-local-ai-v2
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-22
authors:
  - given-names: PLACEHOLDER-OWNER-GIVEN-NAMES
    family-names: PLACEHOLDER-OWNER-FAMILY-NAMES
    affiliation: PLACEHOLDER-OWNER-AFFILIATION
    # orcid: PLACEHOLDER-OWNER-ORCID (https://orcid.org/NNNN-NNNN-NNNN-NNNN, or delete this line)
repository-code: https://github.com/Aliquanto3/wave_local_ai_v2
# MIT covers the code (LICENSE); CC-BY 4.0 covers the data parts LICENSE-DATA
# names. Neither licence covers what LICENSE-DATA says it does not grant.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
